{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "main_title",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# 🧠 Comedy OS — Stand-Up Beliefs Engine\n### *Dual-Pathway Cognitive Architecture: Productive Mastery vs. Destructive Traps*\n\nStand-up mastery requires systematic deconditioning of cognitive distortions and adopting an empirical laboratory mindset.\n\n- 🟢 **[[Constructive 'Good' Beliefs|Productive Beliefs Outline]]**\n- 🔴 **[[Destructive_Beliefs|Destructive Beliefs Outline]]**\n- 🗺️ **[[UX/Visual_Architecture_Flowchart|Visual Architecture Flowchart]]**\n- 💥 **[[?? Persona 1 Pain Spectrum - Bombing|Persona 1 Pain Spectrum]]**",
			"x": -450,
			"y": -750,
			"width": 900,
			"height": 220,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# 🟢 Productive (\"Good\") Beliefs That Drive Mastery\n*The operational mindset of elite joke architects (Louis C.K., Carlin, Leno, Silverman, Brennan, Morril)*",
			"x": -2500,
			"y": -460,
			"width": 1600,
			"height": 110,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_note",
			"type": "file",
			"file": "UX/User Research/Beliefs/Constructive 'Good' Beliefs.md",
			"x": -2500,
			"y": -310,
			"width": 780,
			"height": 520,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_principles",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### ⚡ 5 Deep Psychological Pillars (User Research Data)\n\n1. **The stage is a laboratory, not a referendum on my worth** *(Louis C.K. & Sarah Silverman)*\n   - Bombing is neutral chemical test data, not humiliation.\n2. **I am the king of the room; never give the audience the upper hand** *(George Carlin & Helen Mirren)*\n   - Status held by authority relaxes crowds into laughter.\n3. **Protective Delusion (Early) + Low Self-Esteem Listening (Late)** *(Sam Morril & Jay Leno)*\n   - Audacity to start; ego-free humility to edit.\n4. **Silence and discomfort are where growth happens** *(Louis C.K.)*\n   - Standing in 90s dead air breaks panic; kills reliance on cheap tricks.\n5. **Comparison is the thief of joy — privilege the work** *(Jimmy Carr, Neal Brennan)*\n   - Focus entirely on daily writing output and stage reps.",
			"x": -1680,
			"y": -310,
			"width": 780,
			"height": 520,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 1. Bombing is painful but necessary\n- Unavoidable rite of passage & diagnostic tool.\n- Revealing premise/cadence breakdown.\n- **Addressed by:** Silence & Waveform Telemetry",
			"x": -2500,
			"y": 270,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 2. Working out a set is necessary\n- Deliberate sequence, momentum ramps & callbacks.\n- Engineering reps, not haphazard winging.\n- **Addressed by:** Setlist Timeline & State Machine",
			"x": -2120,
			"y": 270,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 3. Explaining context matters\n- Bringing the audience with you on a trip.\n- Clear premise setup in first 10 seconds.\n- **Addressed by:** Delivery Notation & Diff View",
			"x": -1740,
			"y": 270,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 4. Brevity & precision of thought win\n- Economy of syllables; cutting throat-clearing fluff.\n- Maximizing Laughs-Per-Minute (LPM).\n- **Addressed by:** Distraction-Free Pad & Diff Report",
			"x": -1360,
			"y": 270,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 5. Gimmicks need clear purpose\n- Props or strange voices cannot hide weak writing.\n- Purist stand-up craft first.\n- **Status:** Discussion point (Scope boundary)",
			"x": -980,
			"y": 270,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 6. Punching up jokes is vital\n- Layering 3 to 5 tags, alternates & callbacks.\n- Turning 15s chuckle into a 90s showstopper.\n- **Addressed by:** Atomic Bit DB & Dropped Tag Alerts",
			"x": -2500,
			"y": 470,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 7. Asking peers for punch ups\n- Solitude in writing, communal green room feedback.\n- Low-ego listening reveals blindspots.\n- **Addressed by:** AI Co-Writer / Peer Pitching",
			"x": -2120,
			"y": 470,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b8",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 8. Listening to own sets to improve\n- 'The tape never lies' (Glaser, Leno, Maron).\n- Fast-track B-material into A-material.\n- **Addressed by:** Whisper ASR & Tape Chat",
			"x": -1740,
			"y": 470,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "good_b9",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "### 9. Reusing old bits is a problem\n- Clinging to 5-year-old banker hits causes stagnation.\n- Root cause: fear of bombing with raw material.\n- **Addressed by:** Joke State Machine (Retire) & Freshness",
			"x": -1360,
			"y": 470,
			"width": 340,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "feat_diff",
			"type": "file",
			"file": "Comedy_OS_Note_Taker_Vault/31_Visual_Diff_Report.md",
			"x": -2500,
			"y": 700,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 280
		},
